pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% INTEGRATION-TEST: lenient-header-counts
% Regression test: the DIMACS CNF parser returned the variable count the `p cnf`
% header DECLARES rather than the size of the variable space the file uses.
% `src/lib.rs` sizes the variable-name table from that number (`x1..xN`), the
% checker sizes its propagation `Assignment` from the table, and
% `Assignment::{get,set}_lit_value_unchecked` then index a literal read straight
% from the file with `get_unchecked`. Here the header declares one variable and
% the file names variable 5, so every read of that literal was out of bounds --
% undefined behaviour on the accept/reject path -- and, separately, the proof's
% own `x5` interned as a different variable altogether, because the name table
% had no slot at index 5.
%
% The formula is `(x5)`, whose only solution sets x5 true. This proof logs the
% falsifying solution `~x5` and concludes SAT from it, so it must be rejected.
% Before the fix this tree's release build printed `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE` and
% exited 0. Being undefined behaviour, the outcome was not even stable: the
% byte-identical upstream parser at `4bb10c2c` rejects the same input, and the
% `p cnf 1 2 / 5 0 / -5 0` spelling returns the right verdict by accident. The
% companion `correct/version3/cnf_under_declared_counts_lenient` is that second
% spelling, and pins that it still verifies.
%
% The instance carries `lenient-header-counts` because the strict header check
% is what keeps this out of reach under default flags; the sizing fix is
% independent of that flag, as it must be.
%
% It deliberately does NOT carry the wrong-verdict header marker that
% `tests/defect_table.rs` requires a numbered README row for (the exact phrase
% is spelled in that test), even though this tree did print a wrong verdict for
% it. The table's claim is that every
% numbered defect reproduces against a clean build of upstream `4bb10c2c`, and
% this one cannot make that claim: the behaviour is undefined, so the verdict
% is a property of the build rather than of the source. It is written up in
% full in README.md's `--lenient-header-counts` bullet instead.
sol ~x5;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT : ~x5;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
